  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Rutina and separable verbs",
   "texto": [
    "In Dutch many daily verbs are separable: the prefix is separated and placed at the end of the main sentence. «Opstaan» (get up) is conjugated: «Ik sta om zeven uur op» (the «op» prefix goes to the end). The «om»: «om zeven uur» (at seven) preposition is used to indicate the exact time of an action. To indicate the study site: «thuis» (at home)."
   ]
  },
